<title>THAILAND: Thailand says Hong Kong will remain key entrepot.</title>
<headline>Thailand says Hong Kong will remain key entrepot.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh on Monday expressed confidence that Hong Kong would retain its status as a vibrant entrepot in Asia after its handover to China.</p>
<p>Chavalit congratulated China in a message for the smooth transition of Hong Kong, calling it an important historical occasion for the country.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the People's Republic of China, Hong Kong will sustain its distinctive dynamism and further develop as an economic centre, under the 'one country, two systems' policy as proclaimed by Chinese leaders,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-6520642</p>
</text>
